    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but sitting down just feels like waiting to disappear. the fog isnt lifting, it's just getting thicker. when i look over that edge, it doesnt feel scary... it feels quiet. like the only way to actually find peace from the walking is to just stop trying to find a path that isnt there anymore. like the end of the trail is the only part that actually makes sense.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
